{
  "tema": 7000,
  "slug": "participios-adjetivos",
  "titulo": "Past participles as adjectives",
  "subtitulo": "Está cansado, las ventanas abiertas: participles that agree like adjectives.",
  "foto": "t08.jpg",
  "regla": "A past participle (-ado, -ido) can work as an adjective and then agrees in gender and number: cansado, cansada, cansados, cansadas.",
  "comparada_kwiziq": "2026-10-10",
  "secciones": [
    {
      "id": "regla",
      "titulo": "The rule",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "The past participle (**-ado**, **-ido**) isn't only for compound tenses with **haber** (**he comido**, **había llegado**). It can also work as an **adjective**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "As an adjective, it **agrees** in gender and number with the noun:"
        },
        {
          "tipo": "tabla",
          "encabezados": [
            "",
            "Masculine",
            "Feminine"
          ],
          "filas": [
            [
              "singular",
              "obsesionado",
              "obsesionada"
            ],
            [
              "plural",
              "obsesionados",
              "obsesionadas"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "It's very common after **estar**, to describe a state: **está cansado**, **la puerta está abierta**. It can also go right after the noun: **los niños cansados**, **un lugar abandonado**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Irregular participles work the same way: **abierto**, **roto**, **hecho**, **escrito**, **muerto**, **cubierto**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Compare: with **haber**, the participle never changes (**han cerrado la tienda**); as an adjective, it agrees (**la tienda está cerrada**)."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Tip: with **haber** it's frozen; with **estar** or a noun, it comes alive and agrees."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ejemplos",
      "titulo": "Examples",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "ejemplos",
          "lista": [
            {
              "es": "Beto está ==obsesionado== con el dinero.",
              "en": "Beto is obsessed with money."
            },
            {
              "es": "Naomi está ==obsesionada== con el motor.",
              "en": "Naomi is obsessed with the engine."
            },
            {
              "es": "Los niños ==cansados== se fueron a dormir.",
              "en": "The tired kids went to sleep."
            },
            {
              "es": "Llegamos a un lugar ==abandonado==.",
              "en": "We got to an abandoned place."
            },
            {
              "es": "La policía interrogó a las chicas ==arrestadas==.",
              "en": "The police questioned the arrested girls."
            },
            {
              "es": "Las montañas ==cubiertas== de nieve se veían increíbles.",
              "en": "The snow-covered mountains looked amazing."
            },
            {
              "es": "La ventana del carro está ==rota==.",
              "en": "The car window is broken."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
